{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"conversant-cepivorous-mastiff","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\n`rebar claim` (and its library/MCP equivalents) can only claim a ticket whose current status is `open`. `claim_core` (src/rebar/_commands/txn.py, ~L449-455) reads the reduced state and hard-rejects anything else:\n\n```python\nactual_status = state.get(\"status\", \"\")\nif actual_status != \"open\":\n    raise ConcurrencyMismatch(\n        f'Error: cannot claim {ticket_id}: status is \"{actual_status}\", not \"open\" ...'\n    )\n```\n\n## Observed impact\n\nWhile closing landed work we found tickets left in `blocked` status with an assignee already set (e.g. b783, c7d5, f643, 7a03 — assignee joeoakhart@navapbc.com, status blocked). Because `claim` fast-fails on any non-`open` status, there was no supported way to (re)claim these to resume/finish work; the only remaining lever was a raw `transition`. A ticket that legitimately moved to `blocked` (including via Jira reconcile now that `blocked` is a valid live-Jira status) becomes unclaimable even by the agent that should own it.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n`claim` should be able to move a ticket into `in_progress` from ANY non-terminal status (at least `open` and `blocked`; consider `idea` per ticket-model rules), setting/refreshing the assignee to `ticket.default_assignee`, rather than being hard-wired to `open` only.\n\nSpecial consideration — avoid claim duplication:\n- A ticket ALREADY `in_progress` and assigned to SOMEONE ELSE must still raise ConcurrencyMismatch/exit 10 (do not steal an active claim).\n- A ticket already `in_progress` and assigned to the SAME caller should be an idempotent no-op (not a spurious concurrency error).\n- Preserve the parent-first cascade and the atomic single-commit STATUS+EDIT invariant (I2/I8, docs/concurrency.md).\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe status guard in `claim_core` encodes `open` as the sole claimable source status. The allowable-source set should be widened (open + blocked, and any other non-terminal claimable statuses) with in-progress ownership disambiguation, single-sourced with whatever `transition` treats as claimable.\n\n## Notes\n\nOut of scope for the session that discovered this. Filed for later triage.","id":"0449-cf75-bb4b-41fd","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"claim only accepts open-status tickets; cannot re-claim blocked (or other non-terminal) tickets"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787174529349928001,"uuid":"a7e9d5d4-c3e2-454c-a550-719f9f3a2843"}